---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('shopkeep')!;
const lastUpdated = 'August 21, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Privacy Policy — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description={`How ${app.name} collects, uses, and protects your information.`}
  path={`/${app.slug}/privacy`}
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/shopkeep.png"
  socialImageAlt="ShopKeep app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/shopkeep">← {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how {COMPANY.name} (“we”, “us”) handles
      information in connection with the {app.name} application and website
      (the “Service”) — a workshop tool and inventory manager. We aim to
      collect as little as possible and to keep what we do collect private and
      secure.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Account information.</strong> You may sign in with Apple or
        Microsoft. We receive a stable provider identifier and the basic profile
        information that provider makes available, such as your name and email
        address. Apple may provide a private relay address. Apple and Microsoft
        identities remain separate ShopKeep accounts unless a future linking
        feature explicitly joins them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Inventory data you create.</strong> Content you generate in the
        app — such as your tool inventory, categories and brands, storage
        locations, checkout and loan status, maintenance and warranty records,
        photos, attached documents (manuals, warranties, receipts/invoices), and
        valuations — so the Service can catalog your shop and answer questions
        about it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Limited technical data.</strong> Basic operational logs (such as
        request timestamps, AI-call records, and error information) needed to
        run, secure, and troubleshoot the Service.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> collect precise location, contacts, or device
      advertising identifiers, and we do not use third-party advertising or
      cross-app tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide, maintain, and secure your account and the Service.</li>
      <li>
        To catalog your tools and let you search, organize, check out, and
        report on your inventory.
      </li>
      <li>
        To read receipts and invoices you provide and turn them into inventory
        entries, and to answer natural-language questions about your shop.
      </li>
      <li>To diagnose problems and improve reliability and performance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How your information is stored and protected</h2>
    <p>
      Your inventory data is stored in your own per-user, private SQLite
      database — isolated from other users. Information is encrypted in transit
      using HTTPS, and the Service is hosted on Microsoft Azure. Access is
      limited to what is necessary to operate the Service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tool photos and documents are returned only through authenticated,
      account-scoped media routes. The web and native clients use nonpersistent
      media caches and revoke temporary object URLs when they are no longer
      needed. Raw storage paths are not public product links.
    </p>

    <h2>AI processing</h2>
    <p>
      Receipt and invoice parsing, tool enrichment, and natural-language search
      are powered by Anthropic’s Claude. Only the content needed to fulfill your
      request is sent for processing, and it is not used to train third-party
      models.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with
      infrastructure providers that host and secure the Service (for example,
      Microsoft Azure for hosting and identity, and Anthropic for AI
      processing), and only as needed to operate it, or where required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      We retain your information while the selected ShopKeep account is active.
      In the native app, open <strong>Settings → Account &amp; Data</strong> to
      permanently delete that Apple or Microsoft ShopKeep account. After the
      backend confirms deletion, ShopKeep removes the account’s tools, photos,
      documents, checkout and maintenance history, profile, settings, and
      activity or AI records, then clears local credentials, temporary exports,
      media caches, widget data, and search state for that account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting ShopKeep data does not delete the underlying Apple or Microsoft
      account, and it does not delete a separate ShopKeep account made with the
      other provider. You may also request help with access or deletion by
      emailing <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is intended for a general, adult audience and is not directed
      to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be
      reflected by updating the “Last updated” date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>. For
      product help, visit <a href="/shopkeep/support/">ShopKeep Support</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
